<p>By the light of the now brilliant moons I saw that he was but a shadow of his former self, and as he turned from my caress and commenced greedily to devour the dead carcass at my feet, I realized that the poor fellow was more than half starved. I, myself, was in but little better plight, but I could not bring myself to eat the uncooked flesh, and I had no means of making a fire.</p>
<p>For two days I waited there for Kantos Kan, but as he did not come, I started off on foot in a northwesterly direction toward a point where he had told me lay the nearest waterway. My only food consisted of vegetable milk from the plants which gave so bounteously of this priceless fluid.</p>
